cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Phasentic
message: "If you use Phasentic, please cite the release you used, and also POW_COD and the Crystallography Open Database."
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-09
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/qaemu/phasentic"
abstract: >-
  Phasentic identifies crystalline phases in powder X-ray diffraction
  patterns. It searches the CNR POW_COD reference database, fits mixtures of
  up to five phases, and reports ranked hypotheses with full provenance. Its
  validated preset found the exact phase set in 42.5% (Wilson 95% CI
  35.9-49.4%) and the right phase family in 52.0% (45.1-58.8%) of 200 sealed
  held-out Precursor Genome scans. The code was written with Claude Code.
keywords:
  - powder X-ray diffraction
  - phase identification
  - crystallography
  - POW_COD
  - reproducible science
authors:
  - alias: qaemu
